  "weather": {
    "summary": "Early October in Columbia averages a 63\u00b0F morning low and an 80\u00b0F afternoon high, with roughly a 1-in-6 chance of rain on any given day. Ten-year observed high range: 68\u00b0F to 95\u00b0F.",
    "details": "This is a two-wardrobe weekend. Mornings at the first game are genuinely cool \u2014 bring a jacket or warm layer. Afternoons can still reach the low 90s, so bring the full heat kit as well: water, electrolytes, sunscreen, cooling towels. Rain is possible but not likely on any single day. Start hydrating the day before travel. Based on ten years of recorded daily observations for Columbia, SC (2016\u20132025, Open-Meteo historical archive). A reliable daily forecast becomes available around September 28\u201330.",
    "forecastLink": "https://forecast.weather.gov/MapClick.php?lat=34.1269&lon=-81.2404",
